      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It creates a `NullInputStream` with a negative size (`-30`), reads one byte, and verifies that:\n1. The position advances to `1`\n2. The byte value is `0` (the default `processByte()` return)\n\nThe behavior is non-obvious: with a negative size, `position (0) != size (-30)`, so `read()` succeeds rather than hitting EOF. I'll make this intent clear with a descriptive name and comments.The improved test compiled successfully."
